  "description": "ODARIY crystallizes in the cubic crystal system with space group P -4 3 m. Reported CIF formula moiety: C72 H64 Ce10 O44 P12 4+,8(C5 H6 N1 1+),12(N1 O3 1-),12(C2 H6 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 3 O neighbors; Ce2A (Ce) has 3 O neighbors; Ce1D (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2C (Ce) has 3 O neighbors; Ce1F (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2B (Ce) has 3 O neighbors; Ce1H (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce1J (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce1B (Ce) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 5 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.793-3.793 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 104.05-117.38°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula (pyH)8[Ce10O4(OH)4(O3PPh)12(NO3)12]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 12 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
